#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:44
msgid "1. Creating your first snippet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:45
msgid "Go to Impulse Snippets → Add New. Give it a name (just for your own reference), paste your code, choose where it should go (Head, Body, or Footer), then click Publish. That's it — the code is now live on your site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:49
msgid "2. Head, Body, and Footer — what's the difference?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:51
msgid "Head:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:51
msgid "loads before the page content, in the invisible <head> section. Best for tracking codes, fonts, and meta tags."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:52
msgid "Body:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:52
msgid "loads immediately after the page starts rendering. Some tools (like Google Tag Manager) specifically require this placement."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:53
msgid "Footer:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:53
msgid "loads near the very end of the page, after everything else. Good for chat widgets and anything that shouldn't slow down the initial page load."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:58
msgid "3. Code type & Auto-detect"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:59
msgid "Tell the plugin what kind of code you pasted: JavaScript, CSS, HTML/mixed, or Auto-detect. If you choose JavaScript or CSS and your pasted code doesn't already have <script> or <style> tags around it, the plugin adds them for you automatically. Choose HTML/mixed if your snippet already includes its own tags (most tracking/embed codes do) — nothing gets added or changed in that case."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:63
msgid "4. Linking to an external file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:64
msgid "On the snippet editor, choose \"Link to an external file\" instead of \"Paste code\" if you want to load a script or stylesheet that's already hosted somewhere (like a library file), rather than pasting its contents directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:68
msgid "5. Display Conditions — controlling where a snippet appears"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:69
msgid "By default, a snippet appears on every page of your site. In the Display Conditions box, you can instead restrict it to:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:71
msgid "Specific pages or posts — tick the ones you want, use the search box to find one quickly, or paste its link directly."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:72
msgid "Post types — e.g. only on Pages, or only on Posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:73
msgid "Categories — only on blog posts in the categories you pick."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:78
msgid "6. One-click Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:79
msgid "Under Impulse Snippets → Integrations, paste your Google Analytics 4 Measurement ID, Google Tag Manager Container ID, Meta Pixel ID, or Google Ads ID and the correct snippet(s) are created for you automatically — no code needed. If you ever change the ID and reconnect, it updates the same snippet instead of creating a duplicate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:80
msgid "Google Ads conversion tracking: after connecting your AW- ID, add a conversion action by pasting its conversion label (Google Ads shows it when you create the conversion action). You can optionally set a fixed value and currency. The plugin creates a ready-made snippet and takes you to its edit screen — search for the page that counts as the conversion (usually your thank-you page), add it, and Publish. Until you do, the snippet stays a harmless draft."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:81
msgid "Enhanced conversions (for purchases and leads): these work with the tag this plugin installs — no extra code. Just switch them on inside Google Ads under Goals → Conversions → Settings → Enhanced conversions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:85
msgid "7. Turning a snippet on or off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:86
msgid "Every snippet is just a Published (active) or Draft (inactive) item, exactly like a WordPress post. Switch it to Draft to disable it instantly without losing the code, and switch it back to Published to bring it back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:90
msgid "A word of caution:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wpci-docs.php:90
msgid "code you add here runs exactly as written on your live site, with no safety checks. Only paste code from sources you trust, and double-check a snippet on a staging site first if you're unsure."
msgstr ""

